MID_EV00_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_000_m01_001: And so the forces of the underworld claim another\nhuman enclave.
MID_EV00_000_m01_002: Fortuna!
MID_EV00_000_m01_003: Hong Hua. What have you seen?
MID_EV00_000_m01_004: Terrible things. They've razed three settlements in\nthe area today. No one survived.
MID_EV00_000_m01_005: Nothing left to save, then. How cruel.
MID_EV00_000_m01_006: They have no compassion left. 'Tis only the urge to\nkill that drives them now.
MID_EV00_000_m01_021: Gods!
MID_EV00_000_m01_023: It's the same all over. The armies of the underworld\nare slaughtering everything.
MID_EV00_000_m01_024: What's left of humanity is barely hanging on. And I\ndon't know how much longer they can last.
MID_EV00_000_m01_032: Then we ought to hurry before all is lost.
MID_EV00_000_m01_033: We are bound for the forbidden land. Be my guide.
MID_EV00_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_100_m01_001: 'Tis quiet here. I hear only the sands and winds.
MID_EV00_100_m01_002: No human screams, nor stomp of boots, nor crackle\nof flame from burning homes.
MID_EV00_100_m01_003: Ironic, isn't it? That wall was built to keep us in.
MID_EV00_100_m01_004: But today it has made this the safest place in Dagda.
MID_EV00_100_m01_006: Now then. You say you have a heart in need of a\nnew body?
MID_EV00_100_m01_007: I do. Are you the man for the task?
MID_EV00_100_m01_008: I believe I might be. It won't be the first time I've\nprepared a quality body.
MID_EV00_100_m01_009: Really? That is fortunate. 'Twas worth the trip, then.
MID_EV00_100_m01_010: That said, Nuwa is at its limit. Manufacturing a\nMediator puts a large strain on it.
MID_EV00_100_m01_013: If you're right about the source of this heart,\nthen it's worth everything.
MID_EV00_100_m01_014: What I make will transcend life and death, human\nand deity... It has the potential to be our savior.
MID_EV00_100_m01_018: I'm sure Nuwa would love to take part in bringing\nhope to humanity. As would I.
MID_EV00_100_m01_019: The incubation tank is starting up now. I haven't\nused it in a while, but everything seems in order.
MID_EV00_100_m01_020: Once it's ready, I'll insert the heart along with a\nHeart Core so we can begin growing the body.
MID_EV00_100_m01_021: This tank can produce a new body? That's quite\na marvel.
MID_EV00_100_m01_022: I'm surprised there are any Heart Cores left that\nstill work.
MID_EV00_100_m01_024: Just one left, in fact. We're in luck.
MID_EV00_100_m01_025: I'll be using the one in here.
MID_EV00_100_m01_026: What?! But Master Zenon, won't you die?
MID_EV00_100_m01_027: I've hooked up an external connection with Nuwa to\nsupply me some power.
MID_EV00_100_m01_029: It should keep me going long enough to fulfill my\npromise of a savior.
MID_EV00_100_m01_030: Unacceptable! Use my Heart Core instead.
MID_EV00_100_m01_031: What better way to atone for my sins?
MID_EV00_100_m01_034: A better way to atone for your past would be to work\ntoward a brighter future.
MID_EV00_100_m01_035: You have more to live for. Our savior will need\nyour help.
MID_EV00_100_m01_036: Now...to avoid feedback from the heart, I'll place\nthe Heart Core at the dantian.
MID_EV00_100_m01_037: The overall design is similar to Anatolia's.
MID_EV00_100_m01_038: Though to streamline the process, I may have to\nomit the seven-star engine from the celestial wells...
MID_EV00_100_m01_039: Hrk... *cough* *cough*
MID_EV00_100_m01_040: That's enough, Master Zenon. You should rest.\nLet me finish up here.
MID_EV00_100_m01_041: We are creating the savior of this world. That's worth\nthe life of an old man.
MID_EV00_100_m01_042: Everything we have left...myself, Kunlun, and\nNuwa...it all goes into this.
MID_EV00_100_m01_043: I have little time and don't want to second-guess\nwhether I could have done more.
MID_EV00_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_001_m01_025: Mm?
MID_EV00_001_m01_026: What's this? Have you forgotten me so soon?
MID_EV00_001_m01_004: <NCA>"Who are you?"
MID_EV00_001_m01_031: <NCB>"I can't remember."
MID_EV00_001_m01_027: My name is Sothis. I am also called "The Beginning."
MID_EV00_001_m01_028: I woke you up this once so you can make amends.
MID_EV00_001_m01_029: It's fitting that you be the one to act.
MID_EV00_001_m01_005: Know that this land is on the brink of death.
MID_EV00_001_m01_006: Light fades, plants wilt, and through the gates of\nhell the risen dead storm forth.
MID_EV00_001_m01_007: Each day more people die—more cities burn.
MID_EV00_001_m01_008: The souls of those who fall are caught and offered\nto Balor.
MID_EV00_001_m01_030: Does this not strike you as a sorry state?
MID_EV00_001_m01_015: <NCA>"I have to do something."
MID_EV00_001_m01_032: <NCB>"How can I help?"
MID_EV00_001_m01_016: I speak now as The Beginning.
MID_EV00_001_m01_017: You must defeat Balor, the king below, and drive\nhis darkness from this land!
MID_EV00_001_m01_019: It is your karma that you see this through.
MID_EV00_001_m01_020: Returning light to this enshrouded land seems like\na perfect task for you, I think.
MID_EV00_001_m01_021: Your guide will be Fortuna, Voice upon the Peak.
MID_EV00_001_m01_022: Pay heed to what she says.
MID_EV00_001_m01_024: The rest is up to you. Let all drift through the flow\nof time...
MID_EV00_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_002_m01_001: Hmm. Have you come to?
MID_EV00_002_m01_002: I gather you met her and lived to tell the tale?
MID_EV00_002_m01_003: <NCA>"Where am I?"
MID_EV00_002_m01_024: <NCB>"What is going on?"
MID_EV00_002_m01_004: This will be hard to hear, but...you died. Your body\nwas lost—all but the heart.
MID_EV00_002_m01_007: No flesh, no bones, not even a limb to call your own.
MID_EV00_002_m01_009: But the news is not all bad. They are preparing\na new body for you as we speak.
MID_EV00_002_m01_020: Fortuna, there are a few settings we need to go\nthrough for the new body.
MID_EV00_002_m01_021: Ah. 'Twould seem we have choices to make...
MID_EV00_002_m01_022: But no, not us. You should get to decide these\nthings for yourself.
MID_EV00_002_m02: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m15: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m15_001: Tell me truly—how do you feel about insects and\nthe like?
MID_EV00_002_m15_002: <ICA>"I have no problem with them."
MID_EV00_002_m15_003: <ICB>"I actually like them."
MID_EV00_002_m15_004: <ICC>"I can't stand to see them."
MID_EV00_002_m15_005: <ACA>Very well. Then we needn't make any special\nadjustments at this stage.
MID_EV00_002_m15_006: <ACB>Very well. Then we needn't make any special\nadjustments at this stage.
MID_EV00_002_m15_007: <ACC>Ah! Then allow me to ensure you won't have to\nendure the sight of the vile things.
MID_EV00_002_m15_008: <ACC>The details elude me, but apparently it involves a\nfilter in your brain's visual cortex.
MID_EV00_002_m15_Notice: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m15_Notice_Off: <DLG>The setting that changes the appearance of certain enemies is disabled.\n(You can change this in Settings.)
MID_EV00_002_m15_Notice_On: <DLG>The setting that changes the appearance of certain enemies is enabled.\n(You can change this in Settings.)
MID_EV00_002_m06: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m06_001: One last setting—your name.
MID_EV00_002_m06_002: You have been torn free of causality, so you may take\nany name you like.
MID_EV00_002_m07: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m07_001: Ahh, the name of the Blessed Exile from legend.
MID_EV00_002_m07_002: Whether or not you were serious, it suits you.
MID_EV00_002_m12: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m12_001: Oho, that's a fine name you've come up with.
MID_EV00_002_m13: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m13_001: Ah, so that's what you've decided to call yourself.\nYes...'tis growing on me.
MID_EV00_002_m14: <TH>
MID_EV00_002_m14_001: Nothing wrong with that one. I can see why you'd\nwant to choose it.
MID_EV00_002_m11: <EDH>
MID_EV00_002_m11_001: All the settings are in place now. We're ready to start\ngrowing the Mediator's body.
MID_EV00_002_m11_002: And how much time will that take?
MID_EV00_002_m11_004: It's difficult work, but we'll try to hurry it along.\nPlease wait here.
MID_EV00_002_m11_005: There's a backflow! Power is leaking from the\ndamaged area!
MID_EV00_002_m11_006: Hong Hua, block the E34 circuit. Shunt the overflow\nto B56 and monitor it.
MID_EV00_002_m11_007: I hope these two know what they're about.
MID_EV00_002_m11_008: Did you hear all that? It may be some time before\nyour body is finished.
MID_EV00_002_m11_009: As frustrating as it may be, 'tis better to stay quietly\nin there for now.
MID_EV00_002_m11_010: <NCA>"If I must."
MID_EV00_002_m11_011: Come and see me as soon as you are whole.
MID_EV00_002_m11_012: I'll make things ready for you in Dagsion.
MID_EV00_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_003_m01_001: Fortuna, wait! You can't seriously be going back\nto Dagsion.
MID_EV00_003_m01_002: I used a bit too much of my power. I've never been\nquite like the other children.
MID_EV00_003_m01_003: I tire faster than they do. Hence the need to\nhibernate so often.
MID_EV00_003_m01_004: I will sleep in my temple so I'm refreshed and ready\nto support your promised one.
MID_EV00_003_m01_005: But there's an underworld gate in Dagsion. It's\ncrawling with the risen dead. Will you be alright?
MID_EV00_003_m01_006: My temple is well warded against them. There may\nbe nowhere safer.
MID_EV00_003_m01_007: Balor is a fool, but even he has wisdom enough not\nto venture into my domain.
MID_EV00_003_m01_008: He fears her more than any other. 'Tis better for\nhim to let sleeping gods lie.
MID_EV00_003_m01_009: At least, until his plan is complete.
MID_EV00_003_m01_020: You should know that your savior's karma is the\nreason we all find ourselves in such dire straits.
MID_EV00_003_m01_021: It started innocently enough, like the breeze from\na butterfly's wings.
MID_EV00_003_m01_022: But over the long years, happenstance and human\ndesires intertwined.
MID_EV00_003_m01_023: They have crested into a massive wave of causality\nthreatening to crush everything.
MID_EV00_003_m01_024: And so the butterfly must reckon with the\nresult itself.
MID_EV00_003_m01_010: But Fortuna...
MID_EV00_003_m01_011: This goodbye has gone on long enough. You should\nfocus on your work.
MID_EV00_003_m01_012: Complete that body by fair means or foul and bring\nthe promised one to me.
MID_EV00_003_m01_019: Only then can we begin to turn the tide\nagainst Balor.
MID_EV00_003_m01_013: You have my gratitude for lending your aid in spite\nof all that has come before.
MID_EV00_003_m01_014: It's I who should be grateful. You saved me too.
MID_EV00_003_m01_015: With things this far gone, what human wouldn't\ngrasp at any chance to save the world?
MID_EV00_003_m01_016: The fate of everything depends on what you and\nhe can accomplish here.
MID_EV00_003_m01_017: Let's hope there's anything left of the human world\nto save by the time you're done.
MID_EV00_003_m01_018: I get the point. We won't let you down.
MID_EV00_005_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_005_m01_001: Fortuna...I kept my promise to you...
MID_EV00_005_m01_029: I can't believe you used your own life support to\npower the incubation tank...
MID_EV00_005_m01_030: It may have been our only option, but it still feels\nfar too reckless.
MID_EV00_005_m01_002: I gave you the savior... There's nothing left that\nI can do.
MID_EV00_005_m01_003: The rest is in your hands... Please... Save them...
MID_EV00_005_m01_004: <NCA>"I will take up this burden."
MID_EV00_005_m01_005: Thank...you...
MID_EV00_005_m01_006: It's a blessing that Master Zenon was satisfied\nat the end.
MID_EV00_005_m01_007: He wasn't just our captain. He was practically\na father to the people of the village.
MID_EV00_005_m01_009: <NCA>"What do you mean?"
MID_EV00_005_m01_031: <NCB>"Captain?"
MID_EV00_005_m01_011: This is more than just a village.
MID_EV00_005_m01_025: You might not believe this, but it was once a ship\nthat sailed the stars. It was called Nuwa.
MID_EV00_005_m01_026: As our captain, Master Zenon has spent thousands\nof years with the ship.
MID_EV00_005_m01_008: To sleep with it forever might have been how he\nwould have preferred it to happen.
MID_EV00_005_m01_019: Soon this place will sink below the dunes.
MID_EV00_005_m01_020: Everything, no matter how great, returns to earth.\nYou can't fight it.
MID_EV00_005_m01_021: But I want to try. I'm putting my faith in you\nand Fortuna.
MID_EV00_005_m01_022: <NCA>"What should we do next?"
MID_EV00_005_m01_027: We make for Dagsion, the former imperial capital.\nFortuna should be waiting for us there.
MID_EV00_005_m01_028: I promised that I'd bring you to her.
MID_EV00_005_m01_024: So follow me. I'll lead the way.